def finding(n,diagnosis,effect,description,affected,qs,rule,res):return dict(finding_id=f'A{n:03}',episode_id='F02',diagnosis=diagnosis,effect=effect,description=description,affected=affected,source_evidence=[pool[q] for q in qs],applicable_rule=rule,resolution=res)
f=[]
f.append(finding(1,'defensible_alternative','coverage_or_scope','The nominal backport body is retained as a pragmatic contribution proposal in R08 S01 and as technical context in the other annotations. R08 explicitly preserves the descriptive alternative, distinct referenced objects, partial-reversion qualification, and lack of authority. The packet does not require one additional institutional proposition merely from submission of a PR. This is candidate-boundary sensitivity, not a demonstrated omission or inflated authority claim.',[af('R05',['C00']),af('R06'),af('R08',['S01']),af('R11',['F02-C01']),af('R12',['C01']),af('R14',['F02_C01'])],['Q0001'],'Both guides, Records and proposition boundaries: retain independently interpretable candidates and relevant technical context; retain technical alternatives and do not reconstruct unexpressed authority.','Preserve both readings in alignment as a candidate/context boundary alternative. Do not count the backport candidate as an independent recognized rule, and do not score context-only readings as an omission without a new prospective boundary criterion.'))
f.append(finding(2,'criterion_ambiguity','convention_only','The paragraph-replacement suggestion supports a literal hypothetical reviewer-as-editor parse and a pragmatic addressee-as-editor parse. R05/R06/R08 use the former; R11/R12/R14 use the latter and mark the substituted actor inferred while retaining the explicit change verb and object. Both preserve the same proposed paragraph and tentative force. The guides distinguish reconstructed action from inferred force but do not fully specify whether changing the hypothetical performer alone requires pragmatic parse_mode.',[af('R05',['S02']),af('R06',['F02-S02']),af('R08',['S03']),af('R11',['F02-S02']),af('R12',['S02']),af('R14',['F02_S02'])],['Q0014','Q0015','Q0016','Q0017','Q0002'],'Both guides, Grammar and argument roles: literal where action is supplied, pragmatic when an indirect request requires reconstructed action; assess role basis in the selected parse and preserve alternatives.','Preserve both actor analyses as explicit alternatives. For a later version, specify whether performer substitution with an unchanged explicit predicate is a pragmatic parse trigger. Do not retrospectively recode either as a changed institutional conclusion.'))
f.append(finding(3,'execution_failure','convention_only','R14 F02_S03 labels the directly supplied imperative drop as pragmatic even though its own rationale identifies an omitted actor and antecedent-resolved object, not a reconstructed action. The object, clarity purpose, defeasibility, attribution, and reported-only application are otherwise preserved.',[af('R14',['F02_S03'])],['Q0020','Q0023'],'guide_1.txt, Grammar and argument roles: parse_mode is literal when the source directly supplies the action; inferred components do not by themselves replace the action.','Use literal for this focal drop clause while retaining the contextual actor, inferred object, and all qualifiers. This is a parse convention correction, not an altered recommendation or implementation claim.'))
f.append(finding(4,'execution_failure','convention_only','R11 F02-S04 and R12 S04 label the document-the-empty-string-change proposition pragmatic even though document and its object are explicitly supplied and no editing predicate is reconstructed. Their rationales locate the inference in recommendation force and addressee. The drafted content, optional wording, conditions, and technical-versus-institutional distinction survive.',[af('R11',['F02-S04']),af('R12',['S04'])],['Q0073','Q0029','Q0030','Q0031'],'guide_2.txt, Grammar and argument roles: literal when the source directly supplies the action; inferred utterance force does not automatically make an explicitly stated action inferred.','Use literal for the supplied document action; retain inferred addressee and the optional wording. No institutional-type or standing correction follows.'))
f.append(finding(5,'criterion_ambiguity','evidence_basis','For the spelling correction, R06 and R08 classify application as observed from the resulting integrated spelling, while R14 classifies exact observed correction as unresolved because the earlier typo and its location are absent. These are different observation objects: a resulting artifact versus a historically identified correction operation. The rationales state their limits, so neither establishes the missing before/after edit history.',[af('R06',['F02-S01']),af('R08',['S02']),af('R14',['F02_S01'])],['Q0007','Q0043','Q0039','Q0040','Q0044','Q0045'],'guide_1.txt, Application and challenge and Presentation and later disposition: observed application requires evidence of the relevant act or artifact; particular implementation requires claimed patch changes and integration evidence.','Retain the observed requested spelling and unresolved correction chronology as separate claims. A later specification should distinguish observed resulting state from observed transformation. Do not impose an unavailable before/after-history requirement retrospectively on an explicitly artifact-limited claim.'))
f.append(finding(6,'defensible_alternative','evidence_basis','R14 maps the author\'s aggregate update report, corroborated by the reviewer\'s release-note-update report, to each release-note suggestion as context-inferred reported application. R06/R08 retain those reports at broader-proposal scope. R14 explicitly avoids claiming exact patch proof from that report; all three retain unresolved terse replies. The packet supports a qualified inclusion inference, while exact wording and individual reply targets remain unverified.',[af('R06',['F02-S01','F02-S02','F02-S04']),af('R08',['S02','S03','S05']),af('R14',['F02_S01','F02_S02','F02_S04'])],['Q0002','Q0006','Q0032','Q0033'],'guide_1.txt, Recognition and Application: independently assess target, basis, and application; no new mandatory aggregate-report targeting convention is supplied in this guide.','Keep the qualification visible: reported incorporation of the set of changes can contextually include the edit, but cannot verify the exact formulation or resolve fixed/Both. Do not treat reported and observed as interchangeable, or upgrade ordinary assent to expectation recognition.'))
